# ASS soft breaks (FanEdits)

Kdenlive / libass drop everything after a **real newline** inside a `Dialogue:` text field. Multi-line SRT cues must become **one physical ASS line** with soft breaks.

## Hard rules

1. One `Dialogue:` event = **one physical line** in the `.ass` file.
2. Soft line breaks: literal `\N` (backslash + N). Never paste SRT newlines into ASS text.
3. Never write `\r\N` (CR before `\N`) — that also truncates the second line.
4. Keep full Kdenlive header: `[Script Info]` + `[V4+ Styles]` + `[Events]`. Events-only files are rejected as “invalid”.
5. Prefer LF-only ASS files. Do not hand-convert SRT→ASS in a one-off shell/Python snippet.
6. Wire `subtitlesList` to `*.kdenlive.ass`, not `.srt`.

## Required tool

```bash
python3 scripts/rebuild_kdenlive_ass_from_srt.py --scan FanMixes
python3 scripts/rebuild_kdenlive_ass_from_srt.py --fix FanMixes
python3 scripts/rebuild_kdenlive_ass_from_srt.py --ass "FanMixes/.../Title.kdenlive.ass"
```

After any ASS write, confirm `bare_cont=0` via `--scan` (or that a known multi-line cue contains `\N` on one line, e.g. `Well, fuck layman's terms.\NDo you speak English?`).

## Symptom → fix

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---------|--------|-----|
| Second subtitle line missing in preview | Bare LF after first line of Dialogue | `--fix` / rebuild from SRT with `\N` |
| Only first half of a two-line cue shows | Same | Same |
| Cue present in `.srt` but “gone” in Kdenlive | Project pointed at broken `.ass`, or ASS truncated | Point at `.ass`; rebuild |

Do **not** “fix” by deleting the second line or splitting into two cues unless the owner asks — restore the full cue with `\N`.
